&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an IT Support Analyst who leads with AI — someone who doesn&#39;t just use AI tools as productivity boosters but builds, prompts, and iterates on them to fundamentally change how IT support works. You will be the primary hands-on technologist on our St. Louis support team, resolving employee issues while continuously driving down ticket volume through intelligent automation and self-service. This role sits at the intersection of IT operations and AI enablement: you will both close tickets today and help eliminate the need for those tickets tomorrow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities Include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Powered Support Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as primary point of contact for internal employee IT issues via ticket submission, Slack, and in-person walk-ups — with an AI-first triage mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain AI-driven self-service solutions: prompt-engineer Slack bots, configure intelligent auto-responses, and create Jira automation rules that resolve common issues without human touch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously identify high-volume, repetitive tickets and leverage automation and AI to eliminate them at the root.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own knowledge base quality: use AI tools to surface gaps, draft articles, and keep documentation current so employees can self-serve before they ever open a ticket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Support &amp;amp; Escalation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide L1/L2 support for endpoints and standard enterprise apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot hardware, software, and network connectivity issues; escalate complex cases to L3 teams with clear, AI-assisted diagnostic summaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support employee onboarding and offboarding: provisioning accounts, shipping/retrieving devices, and coordinating with HR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with endpoint management tasks — patching, enrollment, policy compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze ticket trends weekly using dashboards and AI-assisted reporting; surface insights to the Service Desk Director.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in problem management: when the same issue recurs, own it to root cause and build the fix — whether that&#39;s a knowledge article, an automation, or an escalated infrastructure change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test and evaluate new AI tools, integrations, and workflows; document what works and share learnings with the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right candidate is intellectually curious, asks questions before assuming, and gets restless when a repetitive problem doesn&#39;t have a solution yet. Technical skills can be learned; this mindset can&#39;t.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and drive: you investigate problems thoroughly, ask why before escalating, and follow threads until you understand them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-first instinct: you already reach for AI tools when you&#39;re stuck, learning something new, or looking for a faster way — and you&#39;ve built something with them, even if small.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator: you can explain a technical issue to a non-technical employee and you thoroughly document your steps, eliminating the guess work for others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset: when something breaks or keeps breaking, you don&#39;t wait for someone to assign it. You pick it up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on IT experience: You’ve spent time in a Service Desk support role— we want to see that you&#39;ve solved real technology problems for real people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with macOS and/or Windows troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Okta, Google Workspace, Jira, or similar enterprise tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to MDM platforms (Intune, Kandji, NinjaOne) or endpoint management concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building automations: Jira Automation, Slack workflows, Python/Bash scripts, or no-code tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CompTIA A+, ITIL Foundations, or equivalent certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional helpdesk role. You will have direct ownership of AI tooling decisions, automation architecture, and the employee support experience for a global SaaS company. You will work alongside engineers, program managers, and leadership who are actively investing in making IT an AI-native function — and you will be a core part of making that real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Related network and security certifications are a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
