&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.netskope.com/company/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Careers at Netskope&lt;/a&gt; to learn more. Follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/netskope&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/netskope/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a detail-oriented and proactive Sales Operations Specialist to support our growing field sales team, with a strong focus on order management and compliance. This role plays a critical part in maintaining the integrity of our sales operations, ensuring that orders are processed accurately, efficiently, and in line with internal policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate thrives in a fast-paced, collaborative environment and is comfortable working across Sales, Finance, Legal, and Channel teams. You should be highly organized, a strong communicator, and confident navigating complex deal structures within a SaaS/subscription-based business model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and validate sales orders, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and adherence to company pricing structures and policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with sales, finance, and legal teams to resolve any discrepancies or issues related to order submission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate reports on order status, order trends, and other relevant metrics to support sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in data cleansing initiatives to ensure the integrity of sales data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the creation of renewal opportunities and quotes for the sales team, ensuring timely and accurate generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to streamline and improve order management processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document best practices and contribute to the development of standard operating procedures (SOPs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the implementation of new tools or systems related to sales operations and order management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a primary point of contact for sales inquiries related to order status, order modifications, and policy clarification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate effectively with internal stakeholders to provide updates and resolve issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide training and guidance to new sales team members on order submission procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform ad-hoc projects and other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Finance, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in sales operations or order management within a high growth technology or cybersecurity company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SaaS/subscription-based sales models strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and self-motivated, with a strong sense of accountability and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize tasks, manage multiple projects simultaneously, and meet deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a publicly traded or IPO-prepared company is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
